passages.text:
 Example images during peroral pancreatoscopy (POP) in four patients with intraductal papillary mucinous neoplasm (IPMN) showing:
a
a clear proximal margin of a main-duct IPMN (MD-IPMN) that was suspicious for malignancy, but was found to be a mixed-type IPMN without any malignancy on pancreatoduodenectomy (see also
Video 1
);
b
a clear image of a visible polypoid lesion in the setting of MD-IPMN, with biopsy revealing focal malignant transformation;
c
the clear fish-egg-like lesions in an MD-IPMN;
d
a very wide side branch in the body of the pancreas, with a nodular mass seen at the opening of the side branch, which showed mild dysplasia on POP-guided biopsy and later pancreatoduodenectomy.
